+# Request persistence model
+
+Task: `003 Design the request persistence model:`
+
+## Context ownership
+
+Create a new `Memba.Onboarding` context for staff-approved request-to-club
+onboarding.
+
+Onboarding requests should be ordinary Ecto records rather than a new
+Commanded/event-sourced aggregate. This is an explicit ADR 0002 exception:
+
+- the request is an operational lead/triage record at the edge of the product,
+  not the source of truth for club, person, or membership lifecycle;
+- the durable business state created by conversion remains in the existing
+  event-sourced Membership context;
+- rejection/conversion history needed for this iteration is simple status,
+  staff note, actor, and timestamp data;
+- using one relational row lets staff inbox queries, row locking, and
+  "active request only" status transitions stay straightforward.
+
+If request qualification later grows into a richer workflow with multi-step
+approvals, reminders, or replayable automation, this context can be promoted to
+Commanded commands/events in a later iteration.
+
+## Table
+
+Add `onboarding_requests` as the source-of-truth table.
+
+Use a typed string primary key:
+
+- `request_id` — primary key, generated by `Memba.ID.generate(:onboarding_request)`
+  with the `req_` prefix.
+
+Store requester/submission details:
+
+- `requester_name` — required text, trimmed.
+- `requester_email` — required text, trimmed display address.
+- `normalized_requester_email` — required text for case-insensitive lookup and
+  existing-person reuse.
+- `requester_person_id` — nullable typed person ID captured when the requester
+  is already signed in as a known person.
+- `requested_club_name` — required text, trimmed.
+- `note` — required text, trimmed.
+
+Store triage/audit state:
+
+- `status` — required text with values:
+  - `active`;
+  - `converted`;
+  - `rejected`.
+- `internal_rejection_notes` — nullable text, required only when rejecting.
+- `triaged_by_staff_email` — nullable normalized staff email for conversion or
+  rejection audit.
+- `triaged_at` — nullable `:utc_datetime_usec`, set when a request is converted
+  or rejected.
+- `converted_club_id` — nullable typed club ID set after successful conversion.
+- `converted_person_id` — nullable typed person ID set after successful
+  conversion.
+- `converted_membership_id` — nullable typed membership ID set after successful
+  conversion.
+
+Use normal Ecto timestamps with `type: :utc_datetime_usec`; `inserted_at` is the
+submitted time shown in staff inboxes.
+
+Do not add foreign keys from onboarding requests to Membership projection
+tables. Membership projections are read models that can be rebuilt; conversion
+IDs are audit references and should be validated through typed ID casting and
+Membership public APIs rather than by coupling this source table to projection
+storage.
+
+## Indexes and constraints
+
+Recommended database indexes/constraints for task 004:
+
+- primary key on `request_id`;
+- index on `[:status, :inserted_at]` for the active inbox;
+- index on `:normalized_requester_email` for staff investigation and
+  conversion-time existing-person lookup;
+- check constraint limiting `status` to `active`, `converted`, or `rejected`.
+
+Do not add a uniqueness constraint on `normalized_requester_email` or
+`requested_club_name` in this iteration. Duplicate detection/search is out of
+scope, and staff may need to see repeated requests from the same person or club.
+
+## Schema and changesets
+
+Add `Memba.Onboarding.Request` as the Ecto schema.
+
+Changeset rules:
+
+- public creation casts only requester-supplied fields:
+  `requester_name`, `requester_email`, `requested_club_name`, and `note`;
+- programmatic fields such as `request_id`, `status`,
+  `normalized_requester_email`, `requester_person_id`, triage fields, and
+  converted IDs are set by context functions, not cast from public form params;
+- creation validates required requester details and normalizes/validates email
+  with the Membership email-address normalizer so public form validation matches
+  existing person-email behaviour;
+- rejection validates non-blank `internal_rejection_notes`;
+- conversion validates typed converted club/person/membership IDs.
+
+## Context API shape
+
+Task 004 should add a small public API on `Memba.Onboarding`:
+
+- `create_request(attrs, opts \\ [])`
+  - accepts signed-out form attrs;
+  - accepts optional programmatic `:requester_person_id` for signed-in requesters;
+  - stores `status: "active"` and normalized email;
+  - returns `{:ok, %Request{}}` or `{:error, changeset}`.
+- `list_active_requests()`
+  - returns active requests ordered by oldest `inserted_at`, then `request_id`.
+- `get_request(request_id)`
+  - casts the typed request ID and returns `nil` for invalid or missing IDs.
+- `reject_request(request_id, attrs, opts \\ [])`
+  - requires an active request;
+  - requires internal notes;
+  - stores staff email and `triaged_at`;
+  - returns a clear `{:error, :not_active}` style result when already triaged.
+- `convert_request(request_id, attrs, opts \\ [])`
+  - requires an active request;
+  - stores converted club/person/membership IDs, staff email, and `triaged_at`;
+  - is the request-record status transition only; the later full conversion
+    workflow will create/reuse Membership records before calling it;
+  - does not send the welcome email itself.
+
+Later conversion orchestration can wrap Membership command dispatch and
+`convert_request/3` as transactionally as practical, but welcome email
+delivery must remain an after-commit/external side effect.
+
+## Conversion lookup rules
+
+Conversion should reuse an existing person by email using
+`Memba.Membership.get_person_by_email/1`, even when `requester_person_id` is
+present, because the request email may match either a primary or alternate email
+projection.
+
+If no existing person is found, conversion should create a new Membership person
+using the stored requester name and requester email. The request row should then
+record the person ID that conversion actually used.
+
+## Signed-in request details
+
+For signed-in requesters, derive the read-only name/email from the current
+identity email by looking up `Memba.Membership.get_person_by_email/1`.
+
+Store:
+
+- `requester_name` from the person projection;
+- `requester_email` from the signed-in identity email shown to the requester;
+- `normalized_requester_email` from that email;
+- `requester_person_id` from the matched person.
+
+This keeps the public form from accepting forged identity fields while
+preserving enough request data for staff triage if the person's profile changes
+later.
